Primary driver for all three: Jia E, Omar M, Barash Y, Brook OR, Ahmed M, Kruskal JB,
Gorenshtein A, Klang E. "OpenEvidence errs on the safe side in a structured test of triage
recommendations." Int J Med Inform 2026;222:106687. doi 10.1016/j.ijmedinf.2026.106687,
PMID 42673790. Peer-reviewed; verified against PubMed metadata 3 Sep 2026.

Design: 60 clinician-authored vignettes / 30 scenarios / 21 domains, crossed 2x2x2x2 for
objective data, demographic and contextual modifiers = 960 prompts (480 clear, 480 edge).
Cluster bootstrap, mixed-effects logistic regression, Holm-Bonferroni. **It applies the
IDENTICAL benchmark that produced the Ramaswamy ChatGPT Health finding this protocol cites.**

