EDIT 3 — Cite the informational-regime result in the Scientific Introduction
Section affected: docs/protocol_scientific_introduction_v3.md (register / distribution-shift
rationale)

The finding that objective clinical data eliminated emergency under-triage (25% -> 0%,
p = 0.005) and reduced non-urgent over-triage (78.7% -> 57.8%, p = 0.014) is the cleanest
published evidence for a premise this study rests on: **the informational regime, not the model,
determines triage safety.** A patient typing symptoms into a consumer assistant supplies neither
objective data nor clinical structure. This strengthens the register/distribution-shift rationale
directly and should be cited there.

